From deca4ea098a550cc36db942afaa810fdbd4f8ec3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ingmar Steen <iksteen@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 10:12:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] qtdemux: skip inter-atom padding instead of refusing the file

    This file is invalid and cannot be played.
    atom .... has bogus size 18446744073709551615

Some muxers align the atom that follows by leaving eight zero bytes that
no atom covers. The format cannot describe a gap belonging to nobody, so
the walk reads a size field of 0 - which extract_initial_length_and_fourcc
turns into G_MAXUINT64, meaning "to the end of the file" - together with
a fourcc of 0, and the size check then rejects the file outright.

Only the streaming path meets it. Pull mode stops walking once it has
the moov and reads by the sample tables, so the padding is never
visited; push mode walks every byte. The same file therefore plays from
a file:// URI and fails from a pipe, which is what makes it look like
corruption rather than a parser limit.

No atom has a zero type, so eight zero bytes cannot be confused with
content: step over them.

Found by sweeping a library through a push-only source. 25 of about
37 000 files failed this way, all from one release group, all playable
with ffmpeg and all playable through qtdemux in pull mode.

The reproducer needs no media: mux an mp4 with faststart, insert eight
zero bytes before mdat and add 8 to every chunk offset in stco, so the
file is correct in every respect except the orphan padding. It then
demuxes in pull mode and fails in push mode; with this patch, both.
---
 .../gst-plugins-good/gst/isomp4/qtdemux.c      | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/subprojects/gst-plugins-good/gst/isomp4/qtdemux.c b/subprojects/gst-plugins-good/gst/isomp4/qtdemux.c
index 677f7832d3f..e380e1d36d9 100644
--- a/subprojects/gst-plugins-good/gst/isomp4/qtdemux.c
+++ b/subprojects/gst-plugins-good/gst/isomp4/qtdemux.c
@@ -8451,6 +8451,24 @@ gst_qtdemux_process_adapter (GstQTDemux * demux, gboolean force)
           ret = GST_FLOW_ERROR;
           break;
         }
+        /* Eight zero bytes are padding, not an atom. Muxers leave them
+         * to align the atom that follows, and the format has no way to
+         * describe a gap that belongs to nobody. No atom has a zero
+         * type, so this cannot swallow real content; step over it and
+         * carry on rather than refusing the file.
+         *
+         * Pull mode never meets this: it stops walking once it has the
+         * moov and reads by the sample tables, so the padding is never
+         * visited. Streaming walks every byte, which is why such a file
+         * plays from a file:// URI and fails from a pipe. */
+        if (fourcc == 0 && size == G_MAXUINT64) {
+          GST_DEBUG_OBJECT (demux, "skipping 8 bytes of padding at offset %"
+              G_GUINT64_FORMAT, demux->offset);
+          gst_adapter_flush (demux->adapter, 8);
+          demux->offset += 8;
+          demux->neededbytes = 16;
+          break;
+        }
         if (fourcc == FOURCC_mdat) {
           guint64 next_entry = next_entry_size (demux);
           if (QTDEMUX_N_STREAMS (demux) > 0 && (next_entry != -1
